            <span>Handles a full bid package</span>
            <span>Shows why it flagged a number</span>
          </div>
          <div class="upgrade-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></div>
          <div class="upgrade-core">
            <small>Test before it reaches the work</small>
            <strong>Useful capability → working upgrade</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="upgrade-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></div>
          <div class="upgrade-outputs">
            <span>Source documents</span>
            <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
            <span>Inputs extracted</span>
            <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
            <span>Pricing approved</span>
            <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
            <span>Bid ready</span>
          </div>
          <p class="upgrade-caption">Nothing improves automatically. New capability earns its place by working inside the system and under the right human control. The outlined step is where a person approves.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="fit">
      <div class="section-shell">
        <div class="section-head reveal">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Fit</p>
          <h2>This works when the problem has consequences.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>The strongest starting points are consequential, repeated, and visible enough to test. The work also needs an internal owner who can open the right doors and help the new way of working take hold.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- @r020:F3 cta-pull: the fit split helps the visitor decide honestly before moving to the final action -->
        <div class="fit-grid reveal">
          <div class="fit-column">
            <h3>A strong fit</h3>
            <ul class="fit-list">
              <li>Your bottleneck limits revenue, capacity, service, or visibility.</li>
              <li>Your problem repeats and crosses people, tools, or decisions.</li>
              <li>Your real work can show whether the build improved it.</li>
              <li>You can open the right systems and move decisions forward.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="fit-column">
            <h3>Probably not a fit</h3>
            <ul class="fit-list">
              <li>You want generic AI training or a list of tools.</li>
              <li>You want software installed without changing the work around it.</li>
              <li>No one on your team has time to make decisions, provide access, or work the new system into the week.</li>
              <li>The problem is not important enough to test in the business.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="fit-action reveal">
          <p>Recognize your business here?</p>
          <a class="cta" href="/book/" data-cta-source="fit">See if you're a fit</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="final-cta" id="decision">
      <div class="section-shell final-inner reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">The decision</p>
        <h2>Name the bottleneck that <span class="no-break">won’t go away.</span></h2>
        <p class="final-support">If you can name it, we can tell you whether it is the right first build—and what that build could change.</p>
        <a class="cta" href="/book/" data-cta-source="decision">See if you're a fit</a>
        <p class="decision-note">Leave with a clear view of the problem, a first read on what it is costing the business, and whether we are the right team to take it on.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <div class="footer-inner">
      <div class="footer-mark">
        <!-- @r020:identity: exact BWM mark used only for recognition at footer scale -->
        <img src="/assets/mark.svg" alt="" width="48" height="48">
        <span>Buildwise Media</span>
      </div>
      <p>Atlanta-based · Serving owner-led companies across the United States</p>
      <p><a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> · <a href="/terms/">Terms</a></p>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script>
    const scenarios = {
      leads: {
        input: "A lead arrives and waits for someone to notice.",
        system: "Capture, route, follow up, and show the next action.",
        note: "The owner can see every opportunity, who owns it, and what happens next.",
        outcomes: ["Lead captured", "Owner assigned", "Follow-up set", "Status visible"],
        receipt: {
          title: "Lead follow-up",
          input: "New lead captured.",
          control: "Routing follows approved ownership rules.",
          output: "Owner and follow-up due time are visible.",
          pass: "Every lead shows an owner and a next action, checked in real follow-up work."
        }
      },
      bids: {
        input: "A bid stalls because the information lives in five places.",
        system: "Collect requirements, organize inputs, build, and track the bid.",
        note: "The system keeps the job facts, decisions, and status together so the work can move.",
        outcomes: ["Inputs together", "Gaps flagged", "Bid built", "Status visible"],
        receipt: {
          title: "Bidding",
          input: "Bid requirements gathered.",
          control: "Pricing and approval decisions remain human-owned.",
          output: "Inputs, status, and next decision are visible.",
          pass: "A bid passes only when missing inputs, who owes them, and the next pricing decision are visible."
        }
      },
      service: {
        input: "A service request disappears between inboxes and spreadsheets.",
        system: "Create the ticket, assign ownership, track progress, and close the loop.",
        note: "The system gives every request an owner, a status, and a visible next step.",
        outcomes: ["Ticket created", "Owner assigned", "Progress tracked", "Loop closed"],
        receipt: {
          title: "Service work",
          input: "Service request captured.",
          control: "Assignment and exceptions follow approved rules.",
          output: "Owner, status, and next step are visible.",
          pass: "An aged request surfaces before the customer has to chase, with current status and the next service action visible."
        }
      },
      reporting: {
        input: "A decision waits because the numbers do not match.",
        system: "Bring the operating facts together and show what needs attention.",
        note: "The system gives leaders one current view of the facts used to make the decision.",
        outcomes: ["Facts joined", "Conflicts shown", "Decision clear", "Action owned"],
        receipt: {
          title: "Reporting",
          input: "Current operating data joined.",
          control: "Leaders choose the facts used to decide.",
          output: "Conflicts and decisions due are visible.",
          pass: "Conflicting numbers are reconciled to one current source before the decision is due."
        }
      }
    };

    const scenarioKeys = Object.keys(scenarios);
    const scenarioButtons = [...document.querySelectorAll(".scenario-button")];
    const receiptButtons = [...document.querySelectorAll(".receipt-choice")];
    const inputText = document.querySelector("#map-input");
    const systemText = document.querySelector("#map-system");
    const mapNote = document.querySelector("#map-note");
    const outcomeLabels = [...document.querySelectorAll(".map-outcomes span")];
    const evidenceReceipt = document.querySelector(".evidence-receipt");
    const receiptExample = document.querySelector("#receipt-example");
    const receiptTitle = document.querySelector("#receipt-title");
    const receiptInput = document.querySelector("#receipt-input");
    const receiptControl = document.querySelector("#receipt-control");
    const receiptOutput = document.querySelector("#receipt-output");
    const receiptPass = document.querySelector("#receipt-pass");
    const receiptSyncNote = document.querySelector("#receipt-sync-note");
    const evidenceReturn = document.querySelector(".evidence-return");
    const systemVisual = document.querySelector(".system-visual");
    const systemMap = document.querySelector("#system-map");
    const scenarioStatus = document.querySelector("#scenario-status");
    const reduceMotion = window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)");
    const coarsePointer = window.matchMedia("(pointer: coarse)");
    let activeScenario = 0;
    let scenarioTimer;
    let transitionTimer;
    let automaticSteps = 0;
    let userSelected = false;
    let scenarioVisible = false;

    function renderScenario(key, fromUser = false, source = "hero") {
      const scenario = scenarios[key];
      activeScenario = scenarioKeys.indexOf(key);
      inputText.textContent = scenario.input;
      systemText.textContent = scenario.system;
      mapNote.textContent = scenario.note;
      outcomeLabels.forEach((label, index) => {
        label.textContent = scenario.outcomes[index];
      });
      receiptTitle.textContent = scenario.receipt.title;
      receiptInput.textContent = scenario.receipt.input;
      receiptControl.textContent = scenario.receipt.control;
      receiptOutput.textContent = scenario.receipt.output;
      receiptPass.textContent = scenario.receipt.pass;
      receiptSyncNote.textContent = fromUser && source === "receipt"
        ? `${scenario.receipt.title} selected here. The system map above now matches ↑`
        : `See ${scenario.receipt.title} in the system map ↑`;
      evidenceReturn.textContent = `See how the ${scenario.receipt.title.toLowerCase()} build is judged ↓`;
      evidenceReceipt.setAttribute("aria-label", `Example of how a ${scenario.receipt.title.toLowerCase()} build is judged`);
      scenarioButtons.forEach((button) => {
        const selected = button.dataset.scenario === key;
        button.setAttribute("aria-selected", String(selected));
        button.setAttribute("tabindex", selected ? "0" : "-1");
      });
      receiptButtons.forEach((button) => {
        const selected = button.dataset.receiptScenario === key;
        button.setAttribute("aria-selected", String(selected));
        button.setAttribute("tabindex", selected ? "0" : "-1");
      });
      receiptExample.setAttribute("aria-labelledby", `receipt-choice-${key}`);
      systemMap.setAttribute("aria-labelledby", `scenario-${key}`);
      if (fromUser && source === "receipt") {
        scenarioStatus.textContent = `${scenario.receipt.title} evidence example selected. Input observed: ${scenario.receipt.input} Pass criterion: ${scenario.receipt.pass} The system map above now shows the same example.`;
      } else if (fromUser) {
        scenarioStatus.textContent = `${scenarioButtons[activeScenario].textContent} example selected. ${scenario.input} ${scenario.system}`;
      }
    }

    function setScenario(key, fromUser = false, source = "hero") {
      window.clearTimeout(transitionTimer);
      if (reduceMotion.matches) {
        systemVisual.classList.remove("is-changing");
        renderScenario(key, fromUser, source);
        return;
      }
      systemVisual.classList.add("is-changing");
      transitionTimer = window.setTimeout(() => {
        renderScenario(key, fromUser, source);
        window.requestAnimationFrame(() => {
          systemVisual.classList.remove("is-changing");
          const signal = systemVisual.querySelector(".map-arrow i");
          signal.style.animation = "none";
          void signal.offsetWidth;
          signal.style.animation = "";
        });
      }, 180);
    }

    function stopScenarioTimer() {
      window.clearTimeout(scenarioTimer);
    }

    function scheduleScenario() {
      stopScenarioTimer();
      if (!scenarioVisible || document.hidden || reduceMotion.matches || userSelected || automaticSteps >= scenarioKeys.length) return;
      scenarioTimer = window.setTimeout(() => {
        automaticSteps += 1;
        activeScenario = (activeScenario + 1) % scenarioKeys.length;
        setScenario(scenarioKeys[activeScenario]);
        scheduleScenario();
      }, coarsePointer.matches ? 14000 : 7600);
    }

    scenarioButtons.forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        userSelected = true;
        stopScenarioTimer();
        setScenario(button.dataset.scenario, true, "hero");
      });
      button.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
        if (!["ArrowLeft", "ArrowRight", "ArrowUp", "ArrowDown", "Home", "End"].includes(event.key)) return;
        event.preventDefault();
        let nextIndex = activeScenario;
        if (["ArrowLeft", "ArrowUp"].includes(event.key)) nextIndex = (activeScenario - 1 + scenarioKeys.length) % scenarioKeys.length;
        if (["ArrowRight", "ArrowDown"].includes(event.key)) nextIndex = (activeScenario + 1) % scenarioKeys.length;
        if (event.key === "Home") nextIndex = 0;
        if (event.key === "End") nextIndex = scenarioKeys.length - 1;
        userSelected = true;
        stopScenarioTimer();
        setScenario(scenarioKeys[nextIndex], true, "hero");
        scenarioButtons[nextIndex].focus();
      });
    });

    receiptButtons.forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        userSelected = true;
        stopScenarioTimer();
        setScenario(button.dataset.receiptScenario, true, "receipt");
      });
      button.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
        if (!["ArrowLeft", "ArrowRight", "ArrowUp", "ArrowDown", "Home", "End"].includes(event.key)) return;
        event.preventDefault();
        let nextIndex = activeScenario;
        if (["ArrowLeft", "ArrowUp"].includes(event.key)) nextIndex = (activeScenario - 1 + scenarioKeys.length) % scenarioKeys.length;
        if (["ArrowRight", "ArrowDown"].includes(event.key)) nextIndex = (activeScenario + 1) % scenarioKeys.length;
        if (event.key === "Home") nextIndex = 0;
        if (event.key === "End") nextIndex = scenarioKeys.length - 1;
        userSelected = true;
        stopScenarioTimer();
        setScenario(scenarioKeys[nextIndex], true, "receipt");
        receiptButtons[nextIndex].focus();
      });
    });

    systemVisual.addEventListener("mouseenter", stopScenarioTimer);
    systemVisual.addEventListener("mouseleave", scheduleScenario);
    systemVisual.addEventListener("pointerdown", () => {
      userSelected = true;
      stopScenarioTimer();
    });
    systemVisual.addEventListener("focusin", () => {
      userSelected = true;
      stopScenarioTimer();
    });
    systemVisual.addEventListener("focusout", stopScenarioTimer);
    reduceMotion.addEventListener("change", scheduleScenario);
    document.addEventListener("visibilitychange", () => {
      if (document.hidden) stopScenarioTimer();
      else scheduleScenario();
    });

    const scenarioObserver = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        scenarioVisible = entry.isIntersecting;
        if (scenarioVisible) scheduleScenario();
        else stopScenarioTimer();
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.55 });
    scenarioObserver.observe(systemVisual);

    const revealObserver = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add("in-view");
          revealObserver.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.12 });

    document.querySelectorAll(".reveal").forEach((element) => revealObserver.observe(element));

  </script>
</body>
</html>
